af5-9d14-f794a09effb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-38355" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/assets/718dd1f38f7c790ab83639f69462b372de6b7e8501c0a4d6ff678340ab4154bd.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- The function is left-continuous at $x=0$\n- The function is right-continuous at $x=0$\n- The function is continuous at $x=0$" :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false.  The function is not left-continuous at $x=0,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)=3\\ne 0=f(0)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=0,$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)=0=f(0)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=0,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not left-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-38355/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38355"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38547"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/assets/188e0169738a08b3d4580b4f5d3a3ab1aedef87a9d1b83f07c1b10686a38c321.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true in relation to the function $y=g(x)$ above?\n\n- The function is left-continuous at $x=0$\n- The function is right-continuous at $x=0$\n- The function is continuous at $x=0$" :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=0,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}g(x)=0\\ne -2=g(0)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=0,$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}g(x)=-2=g(0)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=0,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not left-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-73106/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "73ae6279-4b0f-5ec4-a115-2cee6676413d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73106/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "18bedbb8-0cf6-50c8-80ce-f0fe2d9ee91f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73106/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" :answer/id #uuid "ef40162a-71c7-5198-b7b6-c17d99c73a24" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73106/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "f858f097-4f4a-56aa-8af3-0c184edbf7f3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73106/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "c09554b8-d00c-5e0d-a923-478cbbf96692" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73106/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "52815081-128f-5fc3-8b49-40e19824f539" :answer-field/key 